TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"verdict":"blocked","diagnosis":"Traced the cp-weights checkpoint failure to a receipt-seeding defect in scripts/stage-weights-both.sh that defeats the idempotence guard already living in scripts/stage-weights.sh, so every re-run stamps a fresh ts onto the tracked receipts and the driver correctly rejects the checkpoint. Evidence and mechanism: (1) the driver stderr is \"spec-build-driver: checkpoint command changed tracked files instead of validating the prepared base\" and the worktree diff at base 1e2eef72397ee0a8053ed816a70e25e55e7aa304 is exactly two ts-only edits, results/receipts/weights-coordinator.json 2026-08-29T12:47:30 -> 2026-08-30T07:30:01 and results/receipts/weights-worker.json 2026-08-29T12:47:30 -> 2026-08-30T07:06:56, with shards 131 and bytes 185563854698 unchanged on both nodes; the measurement therefore matches the committed receipt and confirms the overseer's measured fact that the transfer is already complete and no re-copy occurred. (2) scripts/stage-weights.sh contains the correct guard: it loads the receipt at its $1 path and exits 0 without writing when status/shards/bytes match. (3) scripts/stage-weights-both.sh passes a freshly created mktemp -d path ($TMP/weights-coordinator.json) for the coordinator and, for the worker, a remote /tmp/fn-weights-receipt.json on a node that does not carry this repo. Both target paths are always absent, so the guard's json.load raises OSError, falls through, and writes a new time.strftime ts; install_receipt then mv's that file over the tracked results/receipts/weights-<host>.json unconditionally. The guard is thus never exercised against the committed receipt, which is why cp-weights has now burned attempts on this same purity rule. Scope: the fix is a source edit to scripts/stage-weights-both.sh (seed each staged temp path from the committed receipt before invoking stage-weights.sh, or make install_receipt compare the re-measured facts against the existing tracked receipt and skip the mv when status, shards, and bytes agree so the tracked file stays byte-identical), which this checkpoint task cannot perform because its brief forbids modifying the repository and its argv is fixed by the worklist. Verdict rationale: checkpoint tasks never retry under this contract, and the cause is an out-of-task source fix in the staging scripts rather than a machinery or session fault, so this is blocked with an amendment proposal. The secondary \"configured finalMessage capture ... was not projected within 10000 ms\" projection timeout is downstream of the child's exit 1 and is not an independent transient cause.","proposal":{"kind":"amendment-task","paths":["scripts/stage-weights-both.sh"],"goal":"Make the cp-weights checkpoint command pure: re-running bash scripts/stage-weights-both.sh against an already-correct staged base on both nodes must re-measure, compare against the committed receipts, leave every tracked file byte-identical (no fresh ts), and exit 0. Implement this in scripts/stage-weights-both.sh by giving the existing idempotence guard in scripts/stage-weights.sh something to compare against: either copy the committed results/receipts/weights-coordinator.json to the coordinator's staged temp path and scp the committed results/receipts/weights-worker.json to the worker's /tmp/fn-weights-receipt.json before invoking the per-node script, or have install_receipt compare the freshly staged receipt's status, data.shards, and data.bytes against the existing tracked receipt and skip the mv entirely when they agree. Preserve the D12 quarantine behaviour: a fail receipt still lands under results/receipts/failed/weights-<host>.json and the final assert still exits non-zero on any fail. Do not re-copy the weights; both trees already read 185563854698 bytes across 131 shards. Land the script change plus a deterministic pass receipt in the lane commit so the squash stages a non-empty change.","acceptance":[{"id":"checkpoint-command-exits-zero","description":"The checkpoint command succeeds against the already-staged base on both nodes.","argv":["bash","scripts/stage-weights-both.sh"]},{"id":"rerun-leaves-tracked-tree-clean","description":"Running the checkpoint command a second time over the same prepared base rewrites nothing tracked; the receipts under results/receipts must remain byte-identical, in particular the ts fields of results/receipts/weights-coordinator.json and results/receipts/weights-worker.json.","argv":["bash","-c","bash scripts/stage-weights-both.sh && git status --porcelain -- results/receipts && test -z \"$(git status --porcelain -- results/receipts)\""]},{"id":"receipts-report-expected-facts","description":"Both committed receipts still record status pass with 131 shards and 185563854698 bytes.","argv":["python3","-c","import json;\nfor h in ('coordinator','worker'):\n r=json.load(open('results/receipts/weights-%s.json'%h));\n assert r['status']=='pass' and r['data']['shards']==131 and r['data']['bytes']==185563854698, (h, r)\nprint('receipts ok')"]}],"dependencies":[]}}
